1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Repetitive laboratory work becomes an editable automation
design.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Meta gathers equipment and constraints, then compares two
sourced routes.

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:35,000
The researcher chooses before a machine is designed.

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Original Jubilee CAD supplies the fixed source frame.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Meta proposes the insert, layout and bed pose. Code checks them.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:10,000
100 to 120 mm digital bed drop. Source frame and component sizes
stay fixed.

7
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The accepted layout stays intact while the custom bay is added.

8
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,000
A requested temperature is not a measured cooling result.

9
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:30,000
A 450 mm width is rejected for the fixed Jubilee frame.

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
The accepted geometry is rebuilt locally from the portable
project.

11
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Meta proposes bounded extension dimensions for the existing
workstation.

12
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:00,000
The sweep is kinematic: clearance and camera coverage remain
unverified.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Deterministic direct dilutions: 200, 100 and 20 microlitres of
stock.

14
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Layout and inspection stay intact; rack holes follow target
count.

15
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:25,000
The preparation plan is a calculation proposal, not a validated
lab protocol.

16
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:33,000
The same project produces a revision-specific engineering
package.

17
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:41,000
CAD, custom parts, attribution, parts information and assembly
guidance.

18
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Meta interprets and proposes. Deterministic code calculates and
checks.

19
00:02:50,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Next: physical integration and laboratory validation.
